# Wave 6, editor-shell v2a. Two changes to the canvas that the islands force.
#
# Both are consequences of chrome moving OUT of the canvas and onto islands
# that float over it, and neither is optional: without the first, the toolbar
# and the keyboard would zoom about different points; without the second, the
# error banner draws across the three top islands.

file: "packages/editor/src/canvas/canvas.tsx"
doc:
  "The one SVG surface: pan/zoom group, three layers, and the pointer and\n"
  "keyboard entry points.\n"
  "\n"
  "Two changes here, both forced by chrome moving OUT of the canvas onto\n"
  "islands that float over it. Without the first, the toolbar and the keyboard\n"
  "zoom about different points; without the second, the error banner draws\n"
  "across the three top islands."

structs: [
  { name: "CanvasProps"
    change_type: MODIFIED
    doc:
      "Gains `registerCommandContext`, called once on mount with an accessor\n"
      "that returns the live CommandContext.\n"
      "\n"
      "Why it has to exist at all: the islands dispatch commands, and a\n"
      "command needs a CommandContext. Canvas already builds one for its\n"
      "keydown listener, and three of its seven fields are Canvas-private --\n"
      "`rect` is the containerRect signal, `geometry` is a Canvas-local memo,\n"
      "and `beginTextEdit` is a Canvas-local closure that scrolls the target\n"
      "into view and focuses the editor. The shell can reach none of them.\n"
      "\n"
      "The alternative is that app.tsx builds a SECOND context, and that is\n"
      "specifically what must not happen. The zoom commands anchor on\n"
      "`rect`; two contexts means two rects, so clicking + in the zoom island\n"
      "and pressing = would zoom about different points. Nothing would look\n"
      "broken -- it would just drift, which is the expensive kind.\n"
      "\n"
      "An ACCESSOR, not a value: `rect` and `geometry` change on every resize\n"
      "and every scene rebuild, so a context captured once would go stale and\n"
      "the islands would command against an old viewport.\n"
      "\n"
      "This mirrors `registerFocus` on InspectorProps, which is the\n"
      "established way a child hands the shell a handle into itself.\n"
      "\n"
      "REQUIRED, unlike `onFocusInspector` and `onSave` beside it. There is\n"
      "exactly one call site, so requiring it costs nothing, and the failure\n"
      "if it is optional and app.tsx\'s node lands without wiring it is that\n"
      "every island button is permanently dead with no error anywhere -- the\n"
      "precise shape of the focus-inspector incident that\n"
      "command_wiring.test.ts exists to catch. A required prop makes that a\n"
      "compile error instead."
    fields: [
      { name: "diagram",                type: { named: { symbol: "Diagram" } } },
      { name: "layoutEngine",           type: { named: { symbol: "LayoutEngine" } } },
      { name: "scene",                  type: { named: { symbol: "Scene" } } },
      { name: "stylesheet",             type: { named: { symbol: "Stylesheet" } } },
      { name: "theme",                  type: { named: { symbol: "Theme" } } },
      { name: "ui",                     type: { named: { symbol: "UiState" } } },
      { name: "state",                  type: { named: { symbol: "EditorState" } } },
      { name: "onFocusInspector",       type: { arrow: { output: { primitive: VOID } } }, is_optional: true },
      { name: "onSave",                 type: { arrow: { output: { primitive: VOID } } }, is_optional: true },
      { name: "registerCommandContext", type: { arrow: { inputs: [ { arrow: { output: { named: { symbol: "CommandContext" } } } } ], output: { primitive: VOID } } } }
    ]
  }
]

constants: [
  { name: "Canvas"
    change_type: MODIFIED
    doc:
      "Two changes. Everything else -- the pan/zoom group, the three layers,\n"
      "the pointer router wiring, the wheel handler, the keydown listener, the\n"
      "text editor, fit-on-load -- is untouched.\n"
      "\n"
      "1. On mount, call props.registerCommandContext with an accessor\n"
      "   returning the same context object shape the keydown listener builds.\n"
      "   Build it in ONE place and have both the listener and the accessor\n"
      "   read that, rather than writing the literal twice; two literals is\n"
      "   how the two paths drift.\n"
      "\n"
      "2. The `errorVisible` signal, the createEffect that sets it from\n"
      "   scene.error(), and the absolutely-positioned error banner in the\n"
      "   returned JSX are all DELETED.\n"
      "\n"
      "   That banner is at top 8px, left 8px, right 8px -- full width across\n"
      "   the top of the canvas. D13 puts the inspector island at top-left,\n"
      "   the toolbar top-centre and the file island top-right, so the banner\n"
      "   now draws over all three. StateIsland takes the job, bottom-centre,\n"
      "   where nothing else lives.\n"
      "\n"
      "   Deleting it rather than leaving it is the point: app.tsx wires\n"
      "   StateIsland to the same scene.error() signal in this build, so\n"
      "   keeping both means every scene error appears twice."
    type: { unsupported: { reason: RAW_EXPRESSION, source_excerpt: "Component<CanvasProps>" } }
    uses: ["CanvasProps", "CommandContext"]
  }
]
